	(footprint "eurorack:SW_Taiway_200_SPDT"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "2b1eb7ee-52b4-4299-aa25-f364f84c1834")
		(at 4.6 88.0 90)
		(descr "Taiway series 200 sub-miniature SPDT toggle, PCB vertical, M2 PC thru-hole. Fits any 200-MSPx: ON-ON (MSP1), ON-OFF-ON (MSP3), and the momentary variants. Three terminals in a line on 2.54, 10-48 UNS bushing (o4.80 thread, 5.50 high, flat) -> o4.95 panel hole. Body 5.10 (throw axis, X) x 8.10. Pads numbered as the datasheet does: 1 and 3 are the throws, PAD 2 IS THE COMMON and is the centre terminal. Taiway's contact table reads 2-3 / OPEN / 2-1 in this numbering. Shares the throw axis and bushing with SW_Taiway_200_DPDT, so an SPDT and a DPDT sit on the same panel pitch.")
		(tags "toggle switch spdt on-on on-off-on subminiature taiway 200 eurorack")
